# Legal & SEO

Read `.cursor/skills/studyverce-legal/SKILL.md` before editing these files.

## Non-negotiables

1. **Content source** — legal copy lives in `lib/legal/privacy-content.ts` and `terms-content.ts`; pages only render sections.
2. **Canonical paths** — import `/privacy` and `/terms` from `lib/legal/urls.ts` (Google OAuth consent screen must match production).
3. **Last updated** — bump `PRIVACY_LAST_UPDATED` / `TERMS_LAST_UPDATED` on material policy changes.
4. **Feature changes** — when adding data collection, integrations, or user-facing capabilities, update legal copy in the **same task** (see skill trigger map).
5. **Robots** — disallow paths in `lib/seo/robots-disallow.ts`; keep aligned with protected routes + `/auth/`.

## When shipping product changes elsewhere

If your PR touches auth, rooms, AI, music, analytics, billing, or social features but not legal files, still read `studyverce-legal` and update privacy/terms if user-facing disclosures changed.
